[h1]Societal Value Hints[/h1]

Hover a societal value and its tooltip lists everything that pushes it, read from the game's 1.4 files: estate privileges, government reforms, laws and policies (international organization policies included), and every other source the game has.

[b]What the tooltip shows[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]To further push your country:[/b] what it can take now.
[*] [b]Not yet available:[/b] what it can reach later. The mark at the start of the row, such as (IV), shows the conditions on hover, in the game's own words.
[*] [b]Not available to this country:[/b] other countries' privileges, reforms and policies, such as the Statutes of Lithuania or the Ottoman ones. Shown when "Show everything" is on, with the same conditions on hover: you see what exists and who has it.
[/list]

[b]Other sources in the tooltip[/b]
[list]
[*] Buildings in the capital
[*] Religious aspects and religious schools
[*] Employment systems
[*] Parliament issues and parliament types
[*] Cabinet actions
[*] International organizations and special statuses in them
[*] Advances
[*] Missions
[*] Subject types
[*] Estates
[*] Chivalric orders
[*] Standing modifiers: fort, army and navy maintenance, army and navy size and experience, average control, average development, literacy, estate shares of the population
[*] Conditional modifiers: war and peace, attacking and defending, bankruptcy, the fort limit, legitimacy, and pointing the cabinet at this value
[*] Bureaucracy
[/list]

[b]Filter[/b]
Other sources are filtered as well: religious aspects of another religion, organizations you cannot join, missions when missions are disabled, parliament issues of an estate you do not have are hidden. "Show everything" in the Community Mod Framework mod menu shows them all. Glorp UI's "Show Unavailable Suggestions for Pushing Societal Values" switch does the same.

[b]Glorp UI[/b]
Not required. The rows for privileges, reforms and policies use Glorp UI's wording. If you play with Glorp UI (for 1.4, Glorp UI Río Salado), load this mod after it: both change the same tooltip.

[b]Requires[/b]
Community Mod Framework.

[b]Localization[/b]
English, Français, Deutsch, Español, Português do Brasil, Polski, Русский, Türkçe, 简体中文, 日本語, 한국어

[i]The mod and this description were created with the help of an AI. It has been tested as far as was possible.[/i]
